.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Generated index — rebuild with `expt index build`
data/index/*.sqlite
data/index/*.sqlite-journal
data/index/*.parquet

# macOS Finder metadata. This repo is browsed from the Finder inside a Box sync
# folder, so one of these appears in every directory that has ever been opened.
.DS_Store

# Generated tweezers point lists — try_hardware.py writes <name>.tpf to the repo
# root, and a 1 Hz sine at 50 kHz is 50 000 lines / ~1.2 MB. Regenerate, do not
# store. A .tpf kept deliberately as reference belongs in a subdirectory.
/*.tpf

# ── Vendor material — not ours to redistribute ────────────────────────────
# 19 files (manuals, DLLs, quotes) were removed from the *entire* history on
# 2026-08-28; see NOTICE.md. That scrub cleaned the past and left nothing
# standing in the way of committing the same material straight back in, which
# is what these rules are. Each device's vendor/ folder is restored from its
# MANIFEST.yaml: the folder shape is committed, the files never are.
manual/*
!manual/README.md
hardware/*/vendor/*
!hardware/piezo/vendor/dll_adapter.py
reference/quotes/

# Belt and braces: no vendor binary or document format has ever belonged in
# this repository, and each of these has been committed here once already.
*.pdf
*.dll
*.exe
*.msi

# uv.lock — a by-product, not a decision. This rule was written when `.mcp.json`
# launched the MCP server with `uv run`, which writes a lock file for the whole
# dependency tree. Since 2026-09-04 it launches a venv interpreter directly and
# nothing here invokes uv, so nothing generates this file any more — the rule
# stays because the reason it existed has not changed: the requirements*.txt
# files deliberately carry loose bounds, and a committed lock would quietly
# become the real specification.
uv.lock
